=== p.4 K-1 Problem 1
PASS five pictured tetrominoes are the five distinct free tetrominoes
PASS shared sides: square 4, others 3 (16-8=8, 16-6=10)
  can gain a fifth tile without increasing P: {'straight': False, 'square': False, 'L': True, 'T': True, 'zigzag': True}
PASS extension answer: L, T and zigzag can; straight and square cannot
NOTE p.4: the guide says only "the square cannot, while L can fill its missing corner"; T and zigzag can too, and the straight cannot

